WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.521
Many analyses need codes instead of words, like one for male and two for female.

2
00:00:06.521 --> 00:00:11.860
In this lesson, you will learn to recode a column with mutate and if

3
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.674
else, and then turn the codes back into clear labels.

4
00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:17.200
Let's practice recoding together.

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.180
We start from a fresh demographic table with short column names.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.260
In the Gender column, we see the words Male and Female.

7
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.250
I write two notes.

8
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.961
Converting a two choices variable from character to numeric.

9
00:00:58.961 --> 00:01:02.260
And converting it back, from numeric to character.

10
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.642
The tool for changing a column is mutate.

11
00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:10.168
Demographic, arrow, demographic, pipe, mutate.

12
00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:15.220
Inside mutate, we say which column to change: Gender equals.

13
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.117
Then if underscore else.

14
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.633
It needs three parts:

15
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:30.804
a condition, the value if true, and the value if false.

16
00:01:30.804 --> 00:01:32.700
Just like IF in Excel.

17
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.370
The condition:

18
00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:53.220
Gender, double equals, Male. If true: one. If false: two.

19
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.622
Run it, and open the table.

20
00:02:10.622 --> 00:02:13.318
The Gender column now shows one and two.

21
00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:15.340
One for male, two for female.

22
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.103
Now let's go back. Same pattern:

23
00:02:36.103 --> 00:02:38.189
mutate, Gender equals, if else.

24
00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:40.691
But this time the condition is:

25
00:02:40.691 --> 00:02:42.360
Gender, double equals, one.

26
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.640
If true: Male, in quotes. If false: Female, in quotes.

27
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.660
Text needs quotes, numbers don't.

28
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.254
Run it, and the labels are back.

29
00:03:21.254 --> 00:03:27.320
Mutate changes a column, and if else chooses between two values. A powerful pair! Great work.

